The macOS 27 kernel interfaces the macOS kexts bind to and xnu-12377 lacks, each as the macOS 27.3
kernel (26C5035r) behaves where this kernel has the equivalent:
- set_/match_compilation_service_cdhash_with_length, unrestrict_local_signing_cdhash_with_length:
  the iPadOS 27 *_ext calls under their macOS names (the same 64-byte cdhash with its length).
- cluster_update_range_with_callback: cluster_update_range under its macOS name.
- vfs_context_is_strict_content_protection: the 0x8000 I/O policy bit, never set here.
- vnodeop_desc_name: the descriptor's name.
- task_get_sanitizer_config: 0; spawn does not take a sanitizer configuration on this kernel.
- ifnet_enable_synchronous_input: input keeps the input thread; no state to set.
- image4_v2_set_nonce_digest, _roll_nonce, _load_diavlo_root_ca, _load_local_policy: monitor
  commands; with no code signing monitor they fail as the macOS kernel does when the monitor call
  fails (3 for a NULL argument, 0xffff otherwise).
- os_log_coprocessor_with_handle: the coprocessor message path without the per-coprocessor id.
- os_metric_coprocessor: no metrics stream; the record is not logged.
- IOService::CallPlatformFunction (DriverKit, declared as the 27.2 DriverKit SDK declares it, with
  the SERIALIZABLE keyword): iig generates the stub, the dispatch and the call; the kernel
  implementation answers unsupported (no user platform function handlers) and never forwards.
